From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0336-frizti-06-pipeline-key-refresh-skip.patch

Source: 0336-frizti-06-pipeline-key-refresh-skip.patch
vulkan: skip the pipeline key refresh when nothing it reads changed (off by default)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone.

Source: Frizti/Lichii 13a51aeca3 (Dr. Sergio, Lichii PR 166), GPL-3.0-or-later.

EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_CLEAN=1. Every lookup rebuilds the whole key and compares it, more than once a draw.
Dr. Sergio measured about 40 ms a second at 37,700 draws a second on PC. That number does not carry
over. With the switch a compare of the registers Refresh reads replaces the rebuild while they, the
stage hashes, topology and hint are unchanged and no dirty flag Refresh acts on is set. A log line
every 10 s gives the hit rate.

Changed from the source: 1 only, as our other switches. The list needed no change: this tree's Refresh
differs from that base only in how alpha_test_ref is rounded, and that register is watched.

Runs on the PS5: yes, on the back. Worth trying only if the back is the limit.
Hang: no wait added. A missed register would bind the wrong pipeline.
Pool memory: none, a few KiB of register copy.
Checked: the real FixedPipelineState::Refresh on a Mac, 64 feature sets, 3.8 million changes to every
register word outside the list: the key never moved. Taking 7 registers off the list one at a time was
caught each time. PS5-target syntax compile; anchors unchanged. Not run. The lookup itself ran in a
model on a Mac, the patch's code and the real Refresh beside the plain lookup, 96 random feature sets
three times: 3.4 million lookups, 790,000 without Refresh, the same pipeline every time. 8 of 10 faults
put in the lookup were caught; the other two checks are redundant there.

